{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"6b59c26cdaa0d9d6","name":"card_unit_119_grenadier","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_119_grenadier","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"119. GRENADIER","text":"Becomes Veteran if you control 35. GRENADIER.","flavorText":"Both the 35th and 119th Panzergrenadier Regiments were part of the 25th Panzergrenadier Division of the German Wehrmacht during WWII. Originally formed as the 25th Infantry Division, it participated in the Polish Campaign and the Battle of France. In 1940, it was reorganized as the 25th motorized infantry division and joined Operation Barbarossa, the invasion of the Soviet Union. After two years of fighting in the Soviet Union, it became the 25th Panzergrenadier Division in 1943. The division faced heavy losses during battles, including the near destruction near Minsk in 1944. Survivors were reorganized as the 107th Panzer Brigade, which participated in Operation Market Garden. In November 1944, the brigade regained divisional status and became the 25th Panzergrenadier Division again. It fought a delaying action against the US Third Army in France and defended the Maginot Line fortifications. The division also took part in Operation Nordwind which was the last major German offensive on the Western Front. After the failed German offensive the division was sent to defend against the Soviet attack on the Oder north of Berlin. Afterwards many survivors of the division managed to escape to the west and surrender to British or American forces.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":6,"operationCost":2,"attack":6,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_119_grenadier","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_119_grenadier_title","SourceString":"119. GRENADIER","LocalizedString":"119. GRENADIER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":6,"defense":6,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_119_grenadier_text","SourceString":"Becomes Veteran if you control 35. GRENADIER.","LocalizedString":"Becomes Veteran if you control 35. GRENADIER."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_119_grenadier_history","SourceString":"Both the 35th and 119th Panzergrenadier Regiments were part of the 25th Panzergrenadier Division of the German Wehrmacht during WWII. Originally formed as the 25th Infantry Division, it participated in the Polish Campaign and the Battle of France. In 1940, it was reorganized as the 25th motorized infantry division and joined Operation Barbarossa, the invasion of the Soviet Union. After two years of fighting in the Soviet Union, it became the 25th Panzergrenadier Division in 1943. The division faced heavy losses during battles, including the near destruction near Minsk in 1944. Survivors were reorganized as the 107th Panzer Brigade, which participated in Operation Market Garden. In November 1944, the brigade regained divisional status and became the 25th Panzergrenadier Division again. It fought a delaying action against the US Third Army in France and defended the Maginot Line fortifications. The division also took part in Operation Nordwind which was the last major German offensive on the Western Front. After the failed German offensive the division was sent to defend against the Soviet attack on the Oder north of Berlin. Afterwards many survivors of the division managed to escape to the west and surrender to British or American forces.","LocalizedString":"Both the 35th and 119th Panzergrenadier Regiments were part of the 25th Panzergrenadier Division of the German Wehrmacht during WWII. Originally formed as the 25th Infantry Division, it participated in the Polish Campaign and the Battle of France. In 1940, it was reorganized as the 25th motorized infantry division and joined Operation Barbarossa, the invasion of the Soviet Union. After two years of fighting in the Soviet Union, it became the 25th Panzergrenadier Division in 1943. The division faced heavy losses during battles, including the near destruction near Minsk in 1944. Survivors were reorganized as the 107th Panzer Brigade, which participated in Operation Market Garden. In November 1944, the brigade regained divisional status and became the 25th Panzergrenadier Division again. It fought a delaying action against the US Third Army in France and defended the Maginot Line fortifications. The division also took part in Operation Nordwind which was the last major German offensive on the Western Front. After the failed German offensive the division was sent to defend against the Soviet attack on the Oder north of Berlin. Afterwards many survivors of the division managed to escape to the west and surrender to British or American forces."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Fury","EHelpBubbleTypes::Ambush","EHelpBubbleTypes::Trigger","EHelpBubbleTypes::Veteran"],"hasFury":true,"spawnCardName":"card_unit_119_grenadier_vet","soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'explosion_concrete_large_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Explosions_SFX/Cues/explosion_concrete_large_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/Spring2023Candidates/t_119_grenadier.t_119_grenadier","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Doug Post","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/119__GRENADIER.119__GRENADIER","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":352.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_119_grenadier_photo","SourceString":"German soldiers fighting in the streets of Berlin, 1945.","LocalizedString":"German soldiers fighting in the streets of Berlin, 